{title: Throw Out the Lifeline}
{artist: Edward Ufford}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[C]Throw out the lifeline a[F]cross the dark [C]wave — there is a brother whom [D]someone should [G]save;
[C]somebody's brother! O [F]who then will [C]dare to throw out the [G]lifeline, his [C]peril to share?

Chorus
[C]Throw out the [F]lifeline! [C]Throw out the [G]lifeline!
[C]Someone is [F]drifting a[C]way;
[C]throw out the [F]lifeline! [C]Throw out the [G]lifeline!
[C]Someone is [G]sinking to[C]day.
